<title>JAPAN: Teikoku Oil bid-only afer unit finds new gas field.</title>
<headline>Teikoku Oil bid-only afer unit finds new gas field.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Teikoku Oil Co Ltd were bid-only on the Tokyo Stock Exchange on early Tuesday morning after the company's announcement on Monday that a unit found a new gas field off Japan's Pacific coast.</p>
<p>By 0039 GMT, Teikoku Oil was bid-only at 430 yen, compared with Monday's close of 415 yen.  </p>
<p>Teikoku Oil said on Monday its subsidiary Offshore Iwaki Petroleum Co Ltd had sunk a test well earlier this year in an area about 34 km off Iwaki, Fukushima Prefecture, and the well showed a flow of about 300,000 cubic metres of natural gas per day at a depth of 2,400 metres last week.</p>
